<title>HONG KONG: Hopewell up at midday, limited upside seen.</title>
<headline>Hopewell up at midday, limited upside seen.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hong Kong's Hopewell Holdings Ltd ended the morning session higher on Monday, but brokers said concerns over future recurrent income, after the sale of a large part of its stake in its power generating unit were likely to limit the stock's upside.</p>
<p>Hopewell shares closed the morning up HK$0.05 at HK$5.00 after rising to a morning high of HK$5.15. Its power unit, Consolidated Electric Power Asia Ltd (CEPA), ended unchanged at HK$17.95.  </p>
<p>He expected Hopewell shares to consolidate at current levels while the market digests the implications.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong News Room (852) 2843 6370</p>
